// TEST: Tuple Width One (rejects)
// ERROR: BL1004
// There is no 1-tuple in Blade: `(e)` is grouping, not a 1-tuple
// (formalism.md 1275, and Parser.parseParenExpr collapses the single-element
// case). `Tuple<1>` would therefore have to mean something the value language
// cannot write, so the parser refuses it rather than lowering a degenerate
// one-element IRTTuple that nothing could ever fill.
//
// The diagnostic must survive the LET-ANNOTATION slot specifically: all three
// let-parse sites historically swallowed a type-parse failure and re-reported
// at the `=`, which turned this into a misleading "Expected '=' but got ':'"
// pointing at the colon. Parser.parseLetAnnotation propagates BL1004 instead.

let b = 1.0
let t: Tuple<1> = b
// EXPECT: parse failure -- Tuple<N> requires N >= 2
